   "subject": "on shinyapps.io, shiny.min.js.map fails to load",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I have a small survey app that takes information from a user (including address), writes that information to an internal file, then (among other things) uses the leaflet package to generate a map with markers for all who have taken the survey.<div><br></div><div>It works fine locally and on a Shiny Server at my institution (once the shiny user is granted permission to write to the appropriate /srv subdirectory).  But on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792363236794000&amp;usg=AOvVaw39bewa0qRVxP8TdapBhNvA\">shinyapps.io</a> the app fails as soon as a user submits his/her survey responses.  The error is shown in the attached screenshot:  it appears to be a problem loading the map object.</div><div><br></div><div>Any thoughts?</div><div><br></div><div>Homer</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
